# Lowest-precedence defaults for `docker compose up`.
#
# This file is loaded FIRST in the backend service's `env_file:` list, so every
# value here is overridden by ./.env and then by ./Monad_Backend/.env. That
# ordering is the whole point: it lets the compose stack boot with no
# configuration at all, without ever clobbering a real credential you have set.
#
# It exists because the previous compose declared these in the service's
# `environment:` block instead. In Docker Compose `environment:` ALWAYS wins
# over `env_file:`, so `APY_DATABASE_URL=${APY_DATABASE_URL:-postgresql://postgres:postgres@postgres:5432/fortress}`
# silently replaced the real database URL from Monad_Backend/.env with the local
# container's, and the backend died with:
#     Startup failed: password authentication failed for user "postgres"
#
# Rule of thumb for this stack: `environment:` is only for values that MUST
# differ inside the container network (a service hostname, the listen port).
# Anything that could be a real secret or a real endpoint belongs in an env_file.

# ── Local Postgres / Redis shipped by this compose file ──
# Matches the credentials on the `postgres` service. Set APY_DATABASE_URL in
# Monad_Backend/.env to point at a managed database instead; it wins over this.
APY_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://fortress:fortress@postgres:5432/fortress?sslmode=disable
APY_REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379

APY_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=60000
APY_MAX_STALENESS_MS=300000
POSITIONS_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=30000
POSITIONS_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS=60
POSITIONS_STALE_MS=60000
POSITIONS_WALLET_TTL_DAYS=7

# ── Monad ──
# The backend's zod schema already defaults RPC_MONAD to the public endpoint,
# but it is spelled out here so `docker compose config` shows what will be used.
# The public RPC drops connections under load; point this at a dedicated
# endpoint for anything beyond local poking.
RPC_MONAD=https://rpc.monad.xyz
RPC_MONAD_TESTNET=https://testnet-rpc.monad.xyz

# Aave V3 Monad Pool — getMarketId() == "Aave V3 Monad", verified against live RPC.
AAVE_POOL_MONAD=0x69a5F9AD4f96ebf0a0C792dD42a01cC5C0102fef

# FORTRESS contract addresses are deliberately absent. Leaving them unset makes
# the backend use the verified Monad mainnet defaults compiled into
# src/chains/evm/config/monad.ts, and boot.ts refuses to start if a value here
# ever disagrees with what the RPC reports.

# ── CORS ──
# Comma-separated. Read by src/core/api/server.ts, which ALSO always allows
# localhost/127.0.0.1 on any port, *.vercel.app, and app.fortress.exchange — so
# only list additional origins here.
#
# Requests go out with `credentials: "include"`, so an origin that is not
# allowlisted fails the entire call, not just the cookie. If you serve the
# frontend from your own domain, its origin MUST be here or every API call from
# the browser fails with an opaque "blocked by CORS policy".
#
# NOTE: a CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS line in ./Monad_Backend/.env overrides this whole
# value (it is loaded later) — it does not merge. Include every origin there.
CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://fortress.bhattdev.in,https://api.fortress.bhattdev.in

# ── Server ──
PORT=3000
